Tracy changes in src/engine (07/09/2026: "customise the vendored copy so it follows the standard, so every generated
page is produced the same way"; engine 0.1.5):

  · types.ts     DesignTokens adds `colorPrimaryContrast` (text ON the primary colour: white or black by WCAG
                 contrast, 3:1 keeps white) and `colorPrimaryInk` (primary USED AS TEXT on the page background: itself
                 when it reaches 4.5:1, otherwise the darker `colorPrimaryText` step); SeedToken adds
                 `colorPrimaryContrast?` so a system in the library can feed its `--accent-on` in.
  · derive.ts    `relativeLuminance`/`contrastRatio`/`onColor`/`inkColor` (exact WCAG arithmetic) and the two tokens
                 above in the returned table; the seed wins when present.
  · build.ts     `buildBrandSystem(brand, { seed })` — a seed overlay for callers that know more than Brand.
  · artifacts/*  54 places: `color:#fff` / `stroke="#fff"` / `rgba(255,255,255,a)` on a primary background →
                 `var(--brand-color-primary-contrast)` (rgba → `color-mix(... contrast a%, transparent)`);
                 `color: var(--brand-color-primary)` as text → `--brand-color-primary-ink`; the "inverse" button on a
                 primary background = a plate in the contrast colour, text in the primary colour.
  · kit.ts       primary button, tag, pagination, steps: the same rule.

  Measured reason: upstream hard-codes white text on primary; 47/152 systems in the library have an accent that is too
  light (yellow, cream, pale blue — brutalism, binance, clickhouse, agentic, arc…) so the buttons and eyebrows of the six
  artifacts lost their text, while that same system's own `components.html` uses `--accent-on` correctly. From now on
  the six artifacts are readable on all 152 systems and on brands extracted from a URL (with no `--accent-on`, derive
  picks by itself).

Tracy changes in src/engine (07/09/2026, 22:44: "OpenDesign's branding is still in the footer, replace it with Tracy"):

  · artifacts/_shared.ts  adds `creditHtml(brand)` — the last line of an artifact's footer:
                          "Designed by Tracy · Inspired by <name>", the name linking to `brand.sourceUrl`. Wrapped in
                          `<span data-tracy-credit>` because Tracy's text-fill step replaces the brand name in EVERY text
                          node; unmarked, the page would credit the customer themselves for the design they are borrowing.
  · landing.ts · form.ts · email.ts · _shared.ts (newsletter)
                          the four footers that printed `sourceHost(brand)` (giving `opendesign.dev`) switch to `creditHtml`.

  Measured reason: the home page of a customer site printed "© <customer name> · opendesign.dev / Generated brand
  system" — an address the customer cannot open and a machine-generated line. Tracy's `library-brand.mjs` at the same
  time changes the `sourceUrl` of the 152 systems to `https://cowork.tracy.ai/design-inspiration/<id>`, so "Inspired by"
  opens the page that shows that system.

NOT COPIED (deliberately): `index.ts`, `store.ts`, `memory.ts`, `kit-render.ts`, `kit-i18n.ts`, `system.ts`, `design-md-input.ts`
— they hook into the app's daemon (db, project, transcript) or build prompts for an LLM; Tracy does LLM work through the
customer's agent in chat (spec-huong-thiet-ke §4f decision 6). Correction 06/09: the three `*-fallback.ts` files do NOT call
an LLM — they are deterministic harvesters (icon/favicon, og:image + large images, seed CSS) that run before the agent; they
have been copied and are used in the pipeline.

Tracy only adds, and everything it adds lies OUTSIDE `src/` and `contracts/`:

  · index.ts          — entry point collecting the exports of engine + prefetch + provisional + design-md
  · tracy-tokens.ts   — maps the engine's 218 `--brand-*` tokens → the 56 `tokens.css` tokens of the 152 systems (spec-brand-engine §3.1)
  · NOTICE            — this file
  · tsconfig.dts.json — config that generates `dist/types/*.d.ts` (type declarations only) for plugins consuming `dist/index.js`
  · dist/             — single-file ESM build + `types/` (scripts/build-od-brand-engine.mjs), alias `@open-design/contracts` → `contracts/`

The only external import at run time: `undici` (fetch with a custom Agent to block SSRF in safe-fetch.ts).
